UPDATE companies SET description='Maine Solar Solutions was founded in 2012 by Sam Zuckerman, who began the business from a garage in Portland, Maine. The company is now headquartered in Freeport, with operations also in Brunswick, and remains a locally owned enterprise focused on renewable energy installations across the state.

The firm provides full-service solar electric system design, installation, and ongoing maintenance for residential, commercial, and new-construction projects. Its offerings include rooftop and ground-mount solar arrays, battery backup systems, off-grid installations, electric-vehicle charger setup, and general electrical contracting. Since inception, the company has completed over 3,500 solar installations totaling 8.2 megawatts of capacity, covering the equivalent of nearly 20 football fields of rooftop panels.

Customers range from individual homeowners in towns such as Lisbon, Yarmouth, Kennebunk, and Cape Elizabeth to businesses seeking to reduce operating costs through federal tax incentives. The company also works with builders on new-construction projects to integrate solar from the outset.

Zuckerman started the venture to help Mainers lower utility bills and achieve energy independence while reducing environmental impact. Maine Solar Solutions differentiates itself with a 30-year labor and parts warranty, a Maine-based team that handles permitting, utility interconnection, and long-term service, and a track record as one of the state’s longest-operating solar providers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar electric system design", "Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "New construction solar planning", "Battery backup system installation", "Off-grid solar system installation", "Electric vehicle charger installation", "Electrical contracting", "System monitoring and maintenance", "Permitting and utility interconnection management"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "New construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30-year labor and parts warranty on installations", "Maine-based team manages design, permitting, installation, and ongoing service", "Free solar assessment and instant online estimate calculator", "Over 3,500 solar installations completed in Maine since 2012", "8\u201312 year typical return on investment for cash purchases"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 by Sam Zuckerman in Portland, Maine -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Freeport, Maine with operations in Brunswick -> /about-us", "Provides solar electric system design, installation, battery backup, off-grid, EV charger, electrical contracting -> /about-us", "Completed over 3,500 solar installations totaling 8.2 MW since 2012 -> /about-us", "Serves residential, commercial, and new construction customers across Maine -> /about-us", "Offers 30-year labor and parts warranty -> /", "Free assessment and solar calculator -> /", "NABCEP certified professionals mentioned -> /", "LinkedIn page -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Maine Solar Solutions designs, installs, and services solar electric systems, battery backup, and off-grid systems for homes and businesses across the state.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/maine-solar-solutions/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maine-solar-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maine Wood Heat Company operates from Skowhegan, Maine, where Albie and Cheryl (Kemper) Barden founded the business in the late 1970s. What began as a family venture centered on Finnish-style masonry heaters has grown into a multi-brand operation still owned and run by the Barden family. Second-generation co-owner Scott Barden joined full-time in 2005, shifting the model from nomadic installations to in-house artisan manufacturing under one roof.

The company now works through three complementary brands. Maine Oven Craft produces handcrafted wood-fired ovens for residential backyards and commercial kitchens, including pizzerias and fine-dining restaurants. Maine Metalcraft provides metal fabrication, custom design, and low-volume manufacturing, drawing on more than 75 years of collective expertise among its craftsmen. The Masonry Heaters brand delivers site-built brickwork, stone masonry, and fireplace installation for whole-home heating.

Customers range from homeowners seeking a masonry heater as a primary heat source to chefs and restaurateurs who need high-volume wood-fired ovens. The metal fabrication shop serves clients requiring custom-designed parts and short-run production. All work is performed by a small team of builders, designers, welders, and problem-solvers rather than an automated factory line.

The founders frame the business around enduring values of craftsmanship, connection, and respect for natural materials. They emphasize that they are not a factory but a family of artisans, a distinction they say drives the care put into each oven, heater, and fabricated component.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Custom design", "Low-volume manufacturing", "Wood-fired oven building", "Masonry heater construction", "Brickwork", "Stone masonry", "Fireplace installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial food service", "Pizzerias", "Fine dining", "Home heating"], "materials": ["Steel", "Brick", "Stone"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted wood-fired ovens for residential and commercial use", "Metal fabrication, custom design, and low-volume manufacturing", "Site-built masonry heaters, brickwork, and stone masonry", "Family of artisans with decades of experience, not a factory", "Three generations of craftsmanship guiding every project"], "facts_used": ["Founded in late 1970s by Albie and Cheryl Barden in Skowhegan, Maine -> /", "Three brands: Maine Oven Craft, Maine Metalcraft, Masonry Heaters formalized in 2025 -> /", "Scott Barden joined full-time in 2005, shifted to in-house manufacturing -> /", "Team includes Scott Barden (Co-Owner, Designer & Oven Builder), Cheryl Barden Kemper (Founder & Co-Owner), Garrett Veinotte (Shop Manager), Tom Mason (Lead Welder) -> /", "Maine Oven Craft: wood-fired ovens for residential and commercial (pizzerias, fine dining) -> /", "Maine Metalcraft: metal fabrication, custom design, low-volume manufacturing, 75+ years collective expertise -> /", "Masonry Heaters: site-built brickwork, stone masonry, fireplace installation -> /", "Company describes itself as ''not a factory\u2014we''re a family of artisans'' -> /", "Values: craftsmanship, connection, respect for natural materials -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Handcrafted wood-fired ovens for residential and commercial applications. Metal fabrication and custom designs to low volume manufacturing.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maine-wood-heat-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mainstream Green Solutions LLC was founded in 2009 in Wildersville, Tennessee, by navy veteran Ernie Williams. The veteran-owned company began when Williams obtained Sharp Solar Certification and launched the business as a side venture while researching proven solar technologies. In 2012, he added NABCEP PV Installation Professional certification, and the firm transitioned to full-time operation after 13 years.

The company designs, installs, and services photovoltaic and battery storage systems for residential, agricultural, and commercial clients across West Tennessee. Services include system design and engineering, energy consulting, PV system maintenance, EMP protection, and conversion of legacy TVA grid-tie installations to self-consumption with battery backup. Projects range from off-grid tiny homes and mobile hybrid campground power stations to a solar farm in Gibson County and whole-home backup systems starting under $10,000 installed.

Customers include families, farmers, and businesses such as a medical clinic that received a custom installation. The firm also assists rural businesses and farms in securing USDA REAP grants, which can cover up to 50% of system costs for 2024–2025. All installations use equipment from manufacturers like Sol-Ark, for which Mainstream Green holds Gold Installer status.

Williams emphasizes honest, data-driven proposals and a commitment to service: “If we install it, we will service it.” The company avoids chasing technology trends, instead relying on proven components and transparent cost analysis tailored to each client’s unique situation.', certifications=ARRAY['Sharp Solar Certification (2009)','NABCEP PV Installation Professional Certification (2012)','Sol-Ark Gold Installer (2023)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PV system installation", "Battery storage installation", "System design & engineering", "Energy consulting", "PV system service & maintenance", "EMP protection installation", "Off-grid system design and installation", "Whole-home backup power installation", "TVA grid-tie system conversion to self-consumption", "Solar farm installation", "Mobile hybrid power station installation", "USDA REAP grant application assistance"], "industries": ["Residential", "Agricultural", "Commercial", "Healthcare", "Off-grid living", "New construction", "Utility-scale solar"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Sol-Ark inverters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned and operated since 2009", "NABCEP-certified installation professional on staff", "Sol-Ark Gold Installer status", "Lifetime service commitment on installed systems", "Expertise in USDA REAP grant assistance for farms and rural businesses"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 -> /about-us", "Veteran-owned -> /", "President Ernie Williams -> /about-us", "Sharp Solar Certification 2009 -> /", "NABCEP certification 2012 -> /", "Sol-Ark Gold Installer 2023 -> /", "Location Wildersville, Tennessee -> db", "Services: PV installation, battery, design, consulting, service, EMP protection, TVA conversion -> /", "Projects: solar farm Gibson County, mobile hybrid campground, off-grid tiny home, whole-home backup -> /", "Industries: residential, farms, businesses, medical clinic -> /", "USDA REAP grant assistance -> /", "30% Federal Tax Credit -> /", "Commitment: If we install it, we will service it -> /", "Book: Wired For Disaster -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Since 2009, Mainstream Green has been veteran owned and operated, providing our customers with quality, reliable systems designed to last. ... If we install it, we will service it.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mainstream-green-solutions-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Austin, Texas, Mainstream Medical Devices operates as a contract manufacturer and packager specializing in single-use medical devices. The company''s founding year is not publicly disclosed; however, CEO Dana Wilcox joined in April 2019, bringing over 25 years of industry experience and identifying a need for a right-sized supplier in sterile packaging to complement the firm''s focus on disposable instruments.

The company provides contract manufacturing, contract packaging, and its proprietary Build-a-Kit™ assembly service for single-use medical instruments. Its offerings span sterile packaging solutions, manufacturing solutions, and OEM product development, serving medical device companies from concept through commercialization. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are published.

Mainstream serves the medical device industry, targeting original equipment manufacturers and developers of single-use, disposable instruments and sterile packaging. The leadership team includes President Aaron Bailey, with 30-plus years in medical device commercialization; Senior Director of Operations Casey Atkins, an ASQ-certified quality auditor with experience at Smith+Nephew and Integra LifeSciences; and Director of Quality Ken Thoma, whose background covers orthopedics, active implantables, and in-vitro diagnostics.

The firm emphasizes integrity across its people, products, and partners, aiming to raise industry safety and quality standards through innovative packaging and manufacturing solutions. Wilcox has stated the company was positioned to fill a gap for a right-sized supplier that offers personal attention larger providers cannot, while maintaining a proven track record in developing and commercializing medical devices.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract Manufacturing", "Contract Packaging", "Build-a-Kit\u2122 Assembly", "Single-Use Medical Device Manufacturing", "Sterile Packaging", "OEM Product Development"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Single-Use Medical Devices", "Sterile Packaging"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Austin, Texas -> db", "Services: Contract Manufacturing, Contract Packaging, Build-a-Kit\u2122 -> /", "Focus on single-use medical devices and sterile packaging -> /", "CEO Dana Wilcox joined April 2019 with 25+ years experience -> /about", "President Aaron Bailey 30+ years medical device commercialization -> /about", "Senior Director of Operations Casey Atkins 11+ years experience, ASQ certified Quality Auditor -> /about", "Director of Quality Ken Thoma 30+ years experience in orthopedics, active implantables, in-vitro diagnostics -> /about", "Company emphasizes integrity, quality management system, regulatory compliance -> /about", "Dana Wilcox identified need for right-sized supplier in sterile packaging -> /about", "Proven track record developing and commercializing medical devices -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Packaging, Manufacturing, and Single-Use Instruments for the Medical Device Industry", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mainstream-medical-devices' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Major Custom Cable operates from Jackson, Missouri, as an American manufacturer of custom cable assemblies. The company is backed by the Neutrik Group, pairing domestic production with global engineering expertise. Founded as a relationship-driven team, MCC focuses on mission-critical quality for customers that require dependable components and on-time delivery.

The company designs, manufactures, and tests custom cable solutions in-house, covering fiber optic, copper, and hybrid assemblies, wire harnesses, connectivity systems, Ethernet and fiber internet infrastructure, harsh-environment cables, power distribution, and professional audio cables. Capabilities span prototyping through production, with application-specific materials, ruggedized jacketing, EMI/RFI shielding, and pre-terminated fiber options. Every assembly is built and tested internally to meet defined specifications.

MCC serves aerospace, OEM, datacom, telecom, medical, AVL, broadcast, industrial, and defense sectors. Its cables integrate into complex equipment builds, mission-critical aerospace systems, patient monitoring and imaging devices, high-speed data networks, live-event production, and telecommunications infrastructure. The team brings decades of combined experience supporting customers in selecting and specifying the right assemblies for each application.

The company emphasizes in-house quality control, predictable American manufacturing schedules, fast quoting, and direct access to a dedicated sales and technical support team based in Missouri. This approach aims to reduce downtime, simplify installation, and deliver consistent performance where failure is not an option.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly design and manufacturing", "Fiber optic cable assembly (singlemode, multimode, MPO, trunk)", "Copper cabling solutions", "Hybrid fiber/copper cable assemblies", "Wire harness design and manufacturing", "Connectivity systems (fiber and copper)", "Ethernet cable assemblies (Cat, high-speed data)", "Fiber internet infrastructure solutions", "Harsh environment cable solutions (crush-resistant, ruggedized jackets)", "Power distribution cable assemblies", "Professional audio cable assemblies", "End-to-end custom cable design", "Prototyping and production runs", "EMI/RFI shielding", "Ruggedized connectors and interfaces", "Custom jacket materials (abrasion, oil, chemical, UV resistance)", "Pre-terminated fiber cable assemblies", "Custom power cables and assemblies", "Cable solutions for aerospace, defense, industrial, field applications"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "OEM", "Datacom", "Telecom", "Medical", "AVL (Audio, Video, Lighting)", "Broadcast", "Industrial", "Defense"], "materials": ["Fiber optic (singlemode, multimode)", "Copper", "Hybrid fiber/copper", "Specialty cable options", "Ruggedized jacket materials (abrasion, oil, chemical, UV resistant)", "Shielding materials for EMI/RFI protection", "Ruggedized connectors (MPO, trunk, fiber cores)", "Ethernet cable (Cat)", "Power distribution cable materials", "Wire harness materials", "Audio cable materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house quality control and testing on every assembly", "American manufacturing with predictable lead times", "Fast quoting and streamlined prototyping-to-production workflow", "Direct access to Missouri-based sales and technical support team", "Backed by Neutrik Group for global engineering resources"], "facts_used": ["Location: Jackson, Missouri -> db", "Backed by Neutrik Group -> /about-us", "Manufactures custom cable assemblies -> /about-us", "Industries served: aerospace, OEM, datacom, telecom, medical, AVL, broadcast, industrial, defense -> /about-us, /, /capabilities", "Capabilities: fiber optic, copper, hybrid assemblies, wire harnesses, connectivity systems, Ethernet, fiber internet, harsh environment, power distribution, audio cables -> /capabilities", "In-house quality control and testing -> /about-us", "American manufacturing with predictable lead times -> /about-us", "Fast quoting and streamlined builds -> /about-us", "Direct access to sales and technical support team based in Missouri -> /about-us", "Decades of combined experience -> /about-us", "Materials: fiber, copper, hybrid, specialty cables, ruggedized jackets, EMI/RFI shielding -> /capabilities", "No founding year, employee count, cage code, min order, export compliance, languages, social links found -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MCC manufactures custom cable assemblies", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='major-custom-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Make It Grain Woodworks operates from Boise, Idaho, producing hand-crafted furniture and premium cutting boards. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but its website emphasizes a commitment to traditional woodworking methods and domestic materials.

The shop builds living-area, bedroom, and dining or conference tables, along with cutting boards, using kiln-dried hardwood selected board by board. Joinery includes mortise-and-tenon, half-lap, and screw fastening chosen per application. Finishes are applied after extensive prep work, and the shop integrates features such as waterfall mitered joints, beveled edges, secret compartments, soft-close hinges, and wireless charging pads. All work is described as custom, with clients involved in the design process.

The company positions itself against mass-produced imports that use engineered wood and low-wage overseas labor.

The stated differentiation rests on material quality, joinery variety, finish preparation, and collaborative design.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Mortise and tenon joinery", "Half-lap joinery", "Screw fastening", "Wood finishing (prep and top-shelf application)", "Cutting board fabrication", "Waterfall mitered joints", "Beveled edges", "Secret compartment fabrication", "Soft-close hinge installation", "Wireless charging integration"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom woodworking", "Commercial furniture", "Kitchenware"], "materials": ["Hardwood (kiln-dried)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-selected kiln-dried hardwood", "Multiple joinery methods (mortise-and-tenon, half-lap, screw)", "Extensive finish prep with top-shelf coatings", "Custom design collaboration with each client", "Integrated features: waterfall miters, secret compartments, wireless charging"], "facts_used": ["Location: Boise, Idaho -> db", "Products: hand-crafted furniture (living area, bedroom, dining/conference tables), premium cutting boards -> /", "Materials: kiln-dried hardwood, hand-selected -> /", "Joinery methods: mortise-and-tenon, half-lap, screw -> /", "Finish process: extensive prep, top-shelf finishes -> /", "Custom design collaboration -> /", "Features: waterfall mitered joints, beveled edges, secret compartments, soft-close hinges, wireless charging -> /", "Positioning against mass-produced imports using engineered wood and overseas labor -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Hand Crafted Furniture", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='make-it-grain-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Manchester Molding & Mfg. Co., Inc. has operated in Manchester, Connecticut since 1967. The family-owned business began with a focus on in-house mold design, building, and thermoplastic injection molding, and has continued under the same ownership for over five decades.

The company specializes in custom injection molding, including temporary molds and short production runs. Its capabilities extend to in-house mold design and construction, supported by a tool room equipped with a CNC bed-type mill with three-axis conversational control and additional CNC machine tools. Production runs on vertical, horizontal, and shuttle-type injection molding presses ranging from 40 to 500 tons, with round-the-clock scheduling available. Secondary services include ultrasonic welding, pad printing, assembly, and special packaging.

Manchester Molding serves customers across all industries, though the company does not highlight specific sectors or named clients in its public materials.

