UPDATE companies SET description='Mark Lackley Furniture Maker operates from a woodshop in Taftsville, Vermont. The business traces its start to 2006, when founder Mark Lackley built a custom poker table for a hedge-fund manager from Armonk, New York, complete with drink holders fashioned from refurbished brass artillery shells. Lackley, an Atlanta native and Yale graduate who has lived in Vermont since 2001, runs the company with his wife and business partner, Kim. The venture gained momentum after Maine furniture maker Thomas Moser praised the piece at a fine-furnishings show, urging Lackley to produce more.

The shop produces one-of-a-kind, handcrafted poker and game tables. Each piece is built to order, incorporating custom designs such as reversible tabletops that convert between poker and dining or conference use, varied base styles, integrated chip wells, drink holders, and tailored armrests. Work combines traditional woodworking — joinery, veneering, and intricate inlay — with light fabrication, including custom-welded stainless-steel and brass components for hardware and lighting.

Clients span high-net-worth individuals, corporate executives, and entertainment-industry figures. Notable commissions include a table for Guy Laliberté, co-founder of Cirque du Soleil, and a reversible conference/poker table for an executive office. The tables have also been featured in Architectural Digest, the Robb Report, and the New York Times, with most new business arriving through word of mouth.

The founder''s 30 years at the bench, spanning cabinetmaking, welding, and bookbinding, underpin the blend of artistry and engineering that defines each table.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture making", "Woodworking", "Veneering", "Inlay work", "Welding (stainless steel, brass)", "Custom design", "Finishing (high-gloss, specialty coatings)"], "industries": ["Luxury furniture", "Gaming tables", "Custom woodworking", "Executive office furniture"], "materials": ["Hardwoods (sapele mahogany, ebony, burl madrone)", "Veneers", "Inlays", "Figured burls", "Professional felt", "Speed cloth", "Stainless steel", "Brass", "Leather"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom reversible tabletops (poker/dining or conference/poker)", "Handcrafted one-of-a-kind luxury game tables", "Premium materials including figured burls, veneers, and inlays", "Custom-welded stainless steel and brass components", "Featured in Architectural Digest, Robb Report, and New York Times"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 -> /about-us", "Location Taftsville, Vermont -> db", "Custom handcrafted poker/game tables -> /", "Reversible tabletops, custom bases, chip wells, drink holders, armrests -> /", "Materials: hardwoods, veneers, inlays, figured burls, felt, speed cloth, stainless steel, brass -> /", "Thomas Moser endorsement -> /about-us", "Featured in Architectural Digest, Robb Report, New York Times -> /about-us", "Wife Kim as business partner -> /about-us", "Guy Lalibert\u00e9 commission -> /about-us", "30 years woodworking experience -> /about-us", "LLC structure -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "One-of-a-kind, custom handcrafted poker and game tables, meticulously made in Vermont.", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mark-lackley-furniture-maker' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mark Richey Woodworking and Design operates from a 105,000-square-foot facility in Newburyport, Massachusetts. Over four decades it has grown into a national provider of architectural woodwork and corporate furniture, with a division called WallGoldfinger Furniture dedicated to custom workplace furnishings.

The shop combines high-tech tooling — CNC routers, state-of-the-art finishing lines — with traditional hand craftsmanship to produce acoustic panels, curved wood elements, custom trim, staircases, museum displays, window walls, and full wall-paneling systems. On the furniture side it builds boardroom tables, conference and dining pieces, desks, credenzas, lecterns, moot-court furniture, banquettes, and collaborative seating, including the proprietary Doko product line.

Clients span academic, corporate, museum, performing-arts, residential, restaurant, retail, and hospitality sectors. Notable installations include the LEGO Group’s U.S. headquarters in Boston, the CarGurus office, Novartis Biomedical Research’s U.S. headquarters, the Met’s 81st Street Studio, and a Midwest contemporary residence designed by Peter Rose Architects.

The founders frame the business around sustainability — the plant runs on clean-burning biomass heat — and inclusivity, aiming to mentor a new generation of craftspeople from historically marginalized groups. Leadership emphasizes fused art-and-technology craftsmanship, integrated project teams, and a promise to meet deadlines without sacrificing quality.', certifications=ARRAY['Woman-owned certification','Minority-owned certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural woodwork", "Custom furniture manufacturing", "Acoustic panel fabrication", "Curved wood fabrication", "Custom trim and millwork", "Staircase construction", "Museum display fabrication", "Wall paneling systems", "Window wall systems", "Planter seating construction", "Boardroom furniture", "Conference furniture", "Dining furniture", "Desk manufacturing", "Credenza and lectern fabrication", "Moot court furniture", "Banquette and bench seating", "Collaborative workspace furniture", "Product line development (Doko series)", "Sustainable biomass-powered operations"], "industries": ["Academic", "Corporate", "Exterior", "Museums", "Performing arts", "Residential", "Restaurant", "Retail", "Hospitality"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Woman- and minority-owned certified business", "105,000\u2013130,000 sq ft facility blending CNC technology with hand craftsmanship", "Operations powered by clean-burning biomass heat", "Thousands of projects delivered nationwide since 1981", "Integrated team of artisans, engineers, and project managers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 -> /about", "105,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "130,000 sq ft facility -> /capabilities", "Headquarters 40 Parker St, Newburyport, MA -> /about", "Woman and minority owned certified business -> /about", "3,124+ combined years of experience -> /about", "Thousands projects completed nationwide -> /about", "Mark and Teresa Richey founders -> /", "WallGoldfinger Furniture division -> /about", "Architectural capabilities list -> /capabilities", "Furniture capabilities list -> /capabilities", "Industries served list -> /capabilities", "LEGO Group U.S. headquarters project -> /", "Car Gurus project -> /", "Novartis BioMedical Research US Headquarters -> db", "Midwest contemporary residential by Peter Rose Architects -> /capabilities", "Met 81st Street Studio -> /capabilities", "Sustainability: biomass heat -> /about", "Inclusivity commitment -> /about", "Craftsmanship: art and technology fusion -> /about", "Collaboration: integrated team -> /about", "Commitment to deadlines and promises -> /about", "Greg Porfido COO quote -> /capabilities", "Carolyn Hendrie testimonial -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Within our 130,000 square foot facility, we transform your vision into an object of outstanding quality.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Minority-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mark-richey-woodworking-and-design' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Marlex Pharmaceuticals Inc, based in New Castle, Delaware, positions itself as a generics-focused enterprise serving pharmacy buyers and manufacturers seeking distribution channels. The company runs a manufacturing facility designed for production innovation and inflexible quality standards, with packaging lines capable of bottling 200,000 to 400,000 assorted bottles per month. Its capabilities span pharmaceutical and drug distribution, packaging, labeling, heat induction foil sealing, and manufacturing. Quality assurance operates under cGMP regulations, encompassing batch record review, product release, and inspection of incoming components from contract manufacturers and repackagers.

Marlex serves the pharmaceutical, health care, hospital, and retail sectors. Its customer base includes pharmacy buyers aiming to improve their bottom line, pharmaceutical manufacturers seeking new distribution channels, and health care providers requiring reliable drug supply and related services.

